WEBVTT

00:00:01.020 --> 00:00:04.600
After all, it was Arisugawa Nino's fault 
that Yuzu lost his ability to sing.

00:00:04.600 --> 00:00:06.940
Shut up! I can sing!

00:00:06.940 --> 00:00:07.860
Just watch!

00:00:15.400 --> 00:00:19.990
Alice, I want you to keep singing—

00:00:19.990 --> 00:00:21.000
I can't!

00:00:30.170 --> 00:00:34.680
I'll tell Alice

00:00:31.440 --> 00:00:33.510
<i>I want to steal you from Momo.</i>

00:00:35.180 --> 00:00:40.330
that I want her to be the 
vocalist of In NO Hurry.

00:00:35.770 --> 00:00:36.880
<i>Whatever it takes.</i>

00:00:37.980 --> 00:00:39.180
<i>Right now.</i>

00:00:41.060 --> 00:00:43.560
– 1 Year Ago –

00:00:45.450 --> 00:00:47.480
Hey. Looks like you're all here.

00:00:48.560 --> 00:00:50.980
In NO Hurry to Shout.

00:00:52.410 --> 00:00:53.230
Queen.

00:00:55.450 --> 00:00:56.630
Hatter.

00:00:58.070 --> 00:00:59.080
Cheshire.

00:00:59.080 --> 00:00:59.990
And...

00:01:01.160 --> 00:01:02.180
Alice.

00:01:04.580 --> 00:01:06.870
What's the deal with these outfits?!

00:01:07.070 --> 00:01:11.130
Weren't you the ones who said you'd release 
a CD if your identities could be kept safe?

00:01:11.320 --> 00:01:14.300
Looking like that, no one will recognize you.

00:01:14.300 --> 00:01:16.900
Well, yeah. You've got a point.

00:01:16.900 --> 00:01:19.390
No one would guess this is Yuzu-kun.

00:01:23.710 --> 00:01:26.480
So we're going to have 
Yuzu lip sync to your voice.

00:01:26.480 --> 00:01:27.930
That'll make you happy, right?

00:01:27.930 --> 00:01:28.560
Yes.

00:01:30.110 --> 00:01:32.070
I want to sing.

00:01:35.070 --> 00:01:37.740
Jeez, you kids are weirdos.

00:01:37.740 --> 00:01:39.540
I really don't get what you're thinking.

00:01:39.540 --> 00:01:42.500
If you're going to sing, 
you should just be Alice yourself.

00:01:42.500 --> 00:01:44.040
I don't want to do that.

00:01:44.370 --> 00:01:46.190
We don't care what you think of us.

00:01:46.190 --> 00:01:50.750
Now and forever, the vocalist for 
In NO Hurry will be Alice, and Alice alone.

00:01:52.420 --> 00:01:53.460
One more thing.

00:01:53.810 --> 00:01:56.490
This is the only place I can play my songs.

00:01:56.490 --> 00:01:59.470
I won't go easy on anyone 
who tries to break us up.

00:02:01.680 --> 00:02:05.660
Are you trying to threaten the adult 
who's going to grant your wish?

00:02:06.510 --> 00:02:07.480
But...

00:02:08.510 --> 00:02:09.980
I don't dislike that.

00:02:13.210 --> 00:02:18.170
♭04 That Day, We Who Were Hiding 
How We Truly Felt Joined Hands

00:02:24.550 --> 00:02:26.040
<i>I can't sing today, either.</i>

00:02:27.610 --> 00:02:29.200
<i>I've never experienced this before.</i>

00:02:35.280 --> 00:02:38.840
<i>Was Yuzu shouldering 
feelings like these, too?</i>

00:02:52.140 --> 00:02:53.110
Nino.

00:02:53.350 --> 00:02:54.720
Your book's upside-down.

00:02:54.720 --> 00:02:56.290
What's with that expression?

00:02:56.290 --> 00:02:59.150
Weren't you practicing every day?

00:02:59.150 --> 00:03:01.300
Why haven't you been singing lately?

00:03:01.300 --> 00:03:02.400
You're right.

00:03:03.430 --> 00:03:06.390
I applied for that audition, 
too, so I'd better sing.

00:03:07.000 --> 00:03:08.620
What audition do you mean?

00:03:09.790 --> 00:03:11.620
Hey! What audition?

00:03:11.620 --> 00:03:12.950
Kiryuu Momo's.

00:03:13.790 --> 00:03:15.700
I'm going to the same audition!

00:03:15.700 --> 00:03:17.300
Wait, that's not what I mean! Nino!

00:04:06.010 --> 00:04:07.170
Where's Yuzu?

00:04:07.830 --> 00:04:10.310
He hasn't shown up at all recently.

00:04:11.300 --> 00:04:13.310
He hasn't been coming to school either, right?

00:04:13.310 --> 00:04:16.360
Jeez! The pair of them 
just can't get it together!

00:04:16.360 --> 00:04:17.520
Wait, Miou!

00:04:19.680 --> 00:04:20.520
Miou.

00:04:20.790 --> 00:04:22.030
Miou!

00:04:22.650 --> 00:04:24.190
What do you want, Haruyoshi-senpai?

00:04:24.190 --> 00:04:27.550
Why are you so concerned 
about Arisugawa Nino now?

00:04:27.550 --> 00:04:28.740
Because she's a good person.

00:04:28.740 --> 00:04:29.790
Even though she's weird.

00:04:30.110 --> 00:04:33.770
I heard from Yana-chan that you're 
running around auditioning.

00:04:33.770 --> 00:04:35.970
Are you really okay with 
leaving In NO Hurry?

00:04:35.970 --> 00:04:37.190
Perfectly fine!

00:04:37.190 --> 00:04:39.800
It was never my goal to become Alice.

00:04:41.240 --> 00:04:45.930
I want to be a vocalist that Yuzu 
wants from the bottom of his heart.

00:05:01.960 --> 00:05:03.350
What's up, Miou?

00:05:03.350 --> 00:05:05.900
<i>What are you doing, you idiot?!</i>

00:05:06.120 --> 00:05:07.760
<i>What's your problem?!</i>

00:05:07.760 --> 00:05:10.530
Do you know that Nino doesn't sing anymore?

00:05:10.530 --> 00:05:13.210
More importantly, she said 
she's going for an audition!

00:05:13.210 --> 00:05:14.600
What are you screwing around for?

00:05:14.600 --> 00:05:16.300
What are you gonna do if she's accepted?

00:05:16.300 --> 00:05:18.830
I left In NO Hurry because I 
wanted it to survive, you know!

00:05:18.830 --> 00:05:21.050
Are you gonna let someone 
else snatch her away?

00:05:21.050 --> 00:05:22.560
No, I won't.

00:05:22.560 --> 00:05:23.550
Never.

00:05:24.580 --> 00:05:26.400
<i>Thank you, Miou.</i>

00:05:28.090 --> 00:05:28.960
Yeah.

00:05:55.270 --> 00:05:58.500
I'm here in the dark forest

00:06:05.130 --> 00:06:06.130
Amazing.

00:06:06.880 --> 00:06:10.140
It's almost as if Yuzu's singing.

00:06:14.020 --> 00:06:17.020
I'm... singing.

00:06:24.240 --> 00:06:26.320
Thank you, Miou.

00:06:27.770 --> 00:06:28.650
Yeah.

00:06:30.410 --> 00:06:31.810
Yuzu.

00:06:31.810 --> 00:06:34.290
I want to continue making music with you.

00:06:34.290 --> 00:06:36.660
If you need In NO Hurry 
so you can find Alice...

00:06:37.160 --> 00:06:39.570
If you need to keep doing this, then I'm in.

00:06:42.650 --> 00:06:44.650
Sure, I guess I don't mind doing it with you.

00:06:44.650 --> 00:06:45.420
What?!

00:06:45.900 --> 00:06:47.940
Sheesh, there you go again, Yuzu!

00:06:47.940 --> 00:06:49.110
Such a tsundere!

00:06:49.110 --> 00:06:50.480
What's the problem?!

00:07:08.460 --> 00:07:10.180
<i>I couldn't sing today, either.</i>

00:07:11.270 --> 00:07:12.630
<i>Even though I want to sing...</i>

00:07:19.830 --> 00:07:22.040
Good. You're still here.

00:07:22.490 --> 00:07:22.920
Yu—

00:07:22.920 --> 00:07:24.350
What's with that expression?

00:07:24.350 --> 00:07:26.780
Are you still thinking it's all your fault?

00:07:26.780 --> 00:07:29.040
O-Of course I am!

00:07:29.040 --> 00:07:31.680
Didn't I tell you it isn't?! 
Stop being stubborn!

00:07:31.680 --> 00:07:33.830
But if I hadn't started 
screaming back then—

00:07:33.830 --> 00:07:34.800
Here.

00:07:36.370 --> 00:07:38.060
Shut up and listen to this, Alice.

00:07:38.900 --> 00:07:41.700
I made something to keep you from 
ever sniveling about it again.

00:07:41.700 --> 00:07:44.020
I made this song just because 
I wanted you to sing it.

00:07:44.020 --> 00:07:45.470
B-But...

00:07:45.470 --> 00:07:46.820
Cut it out.

00:07:50.770 --> 00:07:52.070
Hurry and put this in.

00:08:22.840 --> 00:08:24.700
<i>An ear-piercing sound.</i>

00:08:24.700 --> 00:08:26.020
<i>Sound. Sound!</i>

00:08:27.040 --> 00:08:28.430
<i>It's sucking me in.</i>

00:08:28.430 --> 00:08:31.290
<i>Further and further!</i>

00:08:50.200 --> 00:08:52.750
<i>I'm... singing.</i>

00:09:00.690 --> 00:09:01.570
<i>Each note.</i>

00:09:04.220 --> 00:09:08.770
<i>Each and every note is telling me to sing.</i>

00:09:12.740 --> 00:09:15.850
<i>I'm sure I can't make myself 
not worry about it at all.</i>

00:09:16.290 --> 00:09:18.880
<i>But I still want to sing, 
even after letting that all sink in.</i>

00:09:19.210 --> 00:09:20.280
Alice.

00:09:21.370 --> 00:09:23.360
Thank you, Yuzu.

00:09:22.300 --> 00:09:23.360
Thank you.

00:09:25.150 --> 00:09:26.390
Did you just say something?

00:09:26.920 --> 00:09:28.490
Uh, Alice...

00:09:29.300 --> 00:09:31.960
Are you free on May 29th?

00:09:31.960 --> 00:09:34.270
I think I'm probably free.

00:09:34.270 --> 00:09:35.700
Um, Alice...

00:09:36.560 --> 00:09:38.840
Th-That song is—

00:09:39.950 --> 00:09:40.840
Oh, sorry.

00:09:44.160 --> 00:09:45.200
Hello?

00:09:45.200 --> 00:09:48.430
<i>Oh, is this Arisugawa Nino-san?</i>

00:09:48.430 --> 00:09:51.460
<i>I'm Kamiyama from Möbius Entertainment.</i>

00:09:52.960 --> 00:09:56.650
<i>Thank you very much for applying 
to audition at our company.</i>

00:09:56.650 --> 00:10:00.840
<i>You've been shortlisted for the final 
screening, to take place on May 29th.</i>

00:10:00.840 --> 00:10:02.280
<i>I'm calling to inform you of that.</i>

00:10:02.280 --> 00:10:03.370
I made it?!

00:10:04.190 --> 00:10:06.990
I made it? To the final screening?

00:10:08.490 --> 00:10:09.340
<i>Momo.</i>

00:10:11.140 --> 00:10:12.680
May 29th.

00:10:13.810 --> 00:10:16.630
W-Will Kiryuu-san be there that day, too?

00:10:17.900 --> 00:10:20.280
<i>Huh? Oh, so she's the one?</i>

00:10:20.820 --> 00:10:23.020
<i>I'm terribly sorry, Arisugawa-san.</i>

00:10:24.070 --> 00:10:26.530
<i>This is very hard to tell you, but...</i>

00:10:26.530 --> 00:10:29.520
<i>Yours is the only audition 
Kiryuu will not be attending.</i>

00:10:31.080 --> 00:10:34.300
<i>"Your singing voice isn't 
good enough to be a guide."</i>

00:10:34.300 --> 00:10:37.280
<i>"It doesn't give me reason enough to 
see you, so I'm not going," he said.</i>

00:10:37.790 --> 00:10:38.680
Nino.

00:10:38.680 --> 00:10:40.450
I hope, one day, we can 
use your song as a guide

00:10:40.750 --> 00:10:42.030
to find each other again.

00:10:42.670 --> 00:10:43.830
<i>A guide...</i>

00:10:44.410 --> 00:10:45.720
<i>I'm sorry.</i>

00:10:44.810 --> 00:10:45.720
Alice?

00:10:45.720 --> 00:10:48.210
<i>Kiryuu can be a bit of a handful at times.</i>

00:10:49.350 --> 00:10:53.240
<i>Oh, but there are a number of other 
judges who have high hopes for you.</i>

00:10:53.240 --> 00:10:54.800
<i>So we do hope you'll come.</i>

00:10:55.190 --> 00:10:56.290
A guide!

00:10:57.730 --> 00:10:58.420
Alice?

00:10:58.760 --> 00:11:01.340
Alice, did you make it to the final screening?

00:11:01.770 --> 00:11:03.970
I see your eyelashes are as 
unruly as ever today, Yuzu.

00:11:03.970 --> 00:11:06.540
Wh-Who cares about my eyelashes?

00:11:06.540 --> 00:11:08.430
Are you using some special eyelash product?

00:11:08.430 --> 00:11:10.170
Would you listen to me?

00:11:10.170 --> 00:11:11.940
I'm asking about the audition!

00:11:15.200 --> 00:11:17.670
I made it... but I'm not going.

00:11:18.170 --> 00:11:19.300
Why not?

00:11:22.140 --> 00:11:25.330
Kiryuu Momo is the real Momo.

00:11:26.620 --> 00:11:29.630
He said my voice wasn't 
good enough to be a guide.

00:11:30.330 --> 00:11:32.240
That it's not reason enough to meet me.

00:11:32.240 --> 00:11:34.220
And I'm the only audition 
he's not going to attend.

00:11:37.910 --> 00:11:39.670
When I entered middle school...

00:11:39.670 --> 00:11:41.550
And when I entered high school,

00:11:41.550 --> 00:11:44.190
I used Momo's words and 
Yuzu's song to support me.

00:11:44.190 --> 00:11:46.970
And I've always sung, 
believing I'd meet them.

00:11:48.210 --> 00:11:49.170
And yet...

00:11:50.200 --> 00:11:51.000
Mo...

00:11:51.860 --> 00:11:52.750
Mo...

00:11:53.550 --> 00:11:54.410
<i>Momo!</i>

00:11:57.040 --> 00:11:58.090
Go.

00:11:59.530 --> 00:12:04.350
Even if he doesn't go, as long as you 
audition, Momo will have to listen, right?

00:12:04.820 --> 00:12:06.920
So go to the audition.

00:12:06.920 --> 00:12:10.750
But you just asked me if I'm free on May 29th.

00:12:10.750 --> 00:12:12.710
Don't worry about that.

00:12:13.540 --> 00:12:15.630
Go and sing for them.

00:12:15.630 --> 00:12:16.880
No!

00:12:17.280 --> 00:12:18.400
Why not?

00:12:18.400 --> 00:12:20.390
This is another chance for him to hear you.

00:12:20.390 --> 00:12:22.050
No! I'm scared!

00:12:23.920 --> 00:12:26.260
Did you think Momo would never change?

00:12:27.310 --> 00:12:29.150
Six years have passed!

00:12:29.150 --> 00:12:30.670
How could he not change?

00:12:32.300 --> 00:12:35.430
Seriously, when it comes to Momo,

00:12:35.430 --> 00:12:36.980
you instantly turn into a wuss.

00:12:40.190 --> 00:12:43.050
I... I said I'm not going, eyelash milk boy!

00:12:43.050 --> 00:12:44.940
What's your deal, straight-banged mask girl?!

00:12:45.970 --> 00:12:47.580
Thanks for the song!

00:12:47.580 --> 00:12:49.330
You're very welcome!

00:12:53.830 --> 00:12:55.530
Am I an idiot?

00:12:55.530 --> 00:12:57.080
Why did I say that?

00:13:01.640 --> 00:13:05.340
It's because she made that face.

00:13:06.600 --> 00:13:07.590
<i>What's with you?</i>

00:13:08.290 --> 00:13:09.770
<i>What's with you, Yuzu?</i>

00:13:09.770 --> 00:13:11.060
<i>You and your long eyelashes!</i>

00:13:19.350 --> 00:13:22.450
Your singing voice isn't 
good enough to be a guide.

00:13:22.870 --> 00:13:25.150
It doesn't give me reason enough 
to see you, so I'm not going.

00:13:27.840 --> 00:13:28.870
<i>Momo.</i>

00:13:34.500 --> 00:13:37.480
<i>There's no reason for me 
to keep singing anymore.</i>

00:13:43.830 --> 00:13:45.100
<i>She isn't here again today.</i>

00:13:48.770 --> 00:13:51.270
<i>She's been absent from school since then.</i>

00:13:53.390 --> 00:13:55.150
I made it... but I'm not going.

00:13:55.150 --> 00:13:56.740
Go and sing for them.

00:14:00.300 --> 00:14:03.190
<i>And that was my chance 
to make her voice mine.</i>

00:14:10.370 --> 00:14:11.150
<i>But...</i>

00:14:14.190 --> 00:14:15.050
<i>But!</i>

00:14:22.410 --> 00:14:23.600
Hey, Eyelashes.

00:14:23.600 --> 00:14:25.210
Don't call me Eyelashes.

00:14:26.000 --> 00:14:27.280
Oh, sorry, Sakaki.

00:14:27.280 --> 00:14:29.590
I forgot the CD I borrowed 
from you the other day.

00:14:29.590 --> 00:14:31.220
It's fine. Give it back whenever.

00:14:33.380 --> 00:14:34.430
Listen...

00:14:34.760 --> 00:14:38.090
Let's say you have two 
really important things.

00:14:38.090 --> 00:14:39.060
And then, say...

00:14:39.410 --> 00:14:42.090
For your own sake, you want only 
one of those things to happen.

00:14:42.090 --> 00:14:43.390
Is that really okay?

00:14:44.680 --> 00:14:46.460
I don't get what you're saying at all.

00:14:47.340 --> 00:14:48.530
Yeah...

00:14:52.520 --> 00:14:54.900
But if they're both important,

00:14:54.900 --> 00:14:57.580
doesn't that mean you 
just have to value both?

00:14:59.730 --> 00:15:01.540
Even though that might be really hard.

00:15:04.200 --> 00:15:06.250
Yeah. Thanks, Sakaki.

00:15:08.600 --> 00:15:10.090
Wh-Why do you look creeped out?

00:15:10.090 --> 00:15:11.400
That's gross, Eyelashes.

00:15:11.400 --> 00:15:12.800
In short, Eyegrosses.

00:15:12.800 --> 00:15:15.200
I said not to call me Eyelashes!

00:15:15.200 --> 00:15:15.990
Eyegrosses.

00:15:15.990 --> 00:15:16.610
Hey!

00:15:35.030 --> 00:15:36.010
Mom!

00:15:36.870 --> 00:15:39.060
Mom, what's going on outside?

00:15:39.060 --> 00:15:41.290
They said they're turning it into a parking lot.

00:15:42.680 --> 00:15:46.350
You can't blame them. It's been six years.

00:15:46.350 --> 00:15:48.210
I guess things always change.

00:15:49.280 --> 00:15:51.220
Six years have passed.

00:15:51.220 --> 00:15:52.900
How could he not have changed?

00:16:05.390 --> 00:16:07.730
What is this?

00:16:08.650 --> 00:16:10.740
Are you stunned?

00:16:11.790 --> 00:16:14.450
How much have you been 
holding back before now?

00:16:14.450 --> 00:16:16.340
This is just wonderful!

00:16:16.340 --> 00:16:20.750
The guitar is like a maelstrom, and the 
pounding bass line sounds awesome, too!

00:16:20.970 --> 00:16:22.620
Right?

00:16:23.520 --> 00:16:26.410
I guess this is what we get when 
he wants Nino-chan to join.

00:16:26.410 --> 00:16:30.630
And if she joins, I think he'll show us 
something even more amazing.

00:16:30.970 --> 00:16:32.750
Satisfied now?

00:16:32.750 --> 00:16:34.510
Let Nino-chan join.

00:16:35.280 --> 00:16:36.510
You don't play fair.

00:16:36.510 --> 00:16:39.520
What can I say after hearing this song?

00:16:39.770 --> 00:16:43.800
All right! We'll bust out 
this new song on May 29th!

00:16:43.800 --> 00:16:44.760
About that...

00:16:45.730 --> 00:16:48.700
Do you think it's possible to put 
the vocals in just before the show?

00:16:48.700 --> 00:16:49.820
Huh?

00:16:59.540 --> 00:17:02.280
<i>I had the idea in my head</i>

00:17:02.280 --> 00:17:04.570
<i>that nothing would ever change.</i>

00:17:04.570 --> 00:17:06.790
<i>But maybe everything changes, like Yuzu said.</i>

00:17:07.980 --> 00:17:10.090
<i>Momo skipped town with his family.</i>

00:17:10.640 --> 00:17:14.120
<i>I wonder if he spent these past six 
years in a way I can't even imagine.</i>

00:17:16.370 --> 00:17:18.300
<i>This is bad. I feel like I'm gonna scream.</i>

00:17:32.110 --> 00:17:32.860
Alice.

00:17:33.980 --> 00:17:36.790
I made this song just because 
I wanted you to sing it.

00:17:41.610 --> 00:17:44.600
<i>Within the maelstrom of guitar 
and the storm of sound,</i>

00:17:44.600 --> 00:17:47.120
<i>I could hear Yuzu's transient melody.</i>

00:17:47.810 --> 00:17:51.130
<i>It sounded a bit like In NO Hurry's songs.</i>

00:17:52.250 --> 00:17:54.410
<i>I wanted to sing it from 
the depths of my heart.</i>

00:17:55.220 --> 00:17:57.700
Momo-kun!

00:17:57.700 --> 00:17:59.800
Let's sing!

00:18:01.230 --> 00:18:02.400
<i>Things that change.</i>

00:18:03.840 --> 00:18:05.170
<i>Things that never change.</i>

00:18:06.550 --> 00:18:10.990
<i>My longing for Momo hasn't 
changed in the slightest.</i>

00:18:11.620 --> 00:18:12.650
<i>What about Momo?</i>

00:18:13.010 --> 00:18:16.060
Your singing voice isn't 
good enough to be a guide.

00:18:16.530 --> 00:18:18.910
It doesn't give me reason enough 
to see you, so I'm not going.

00:18:19.440 --> 00:18:22.660
<i>He flipped around the meaning 
of his words from six years ago.</i>

00:18:26.880 --> 00:18:27.670
Wait...

00:18:28.370 --> 00:18:30.180
If we can't see each other anymore...

00:18:30.730 --> 00:18:34.550
I hope, one day, we can use your song 
as a guide to find each other again.

00:18:36.320 --> 00:18:37.770
Does he mean

00:18:37.770 --> 00:18:39.680
he still remembers that promise?

00:18:44.130 --> 00:18:47.560
<i>Any time I called for Momo, 
he always turned my way.</i>

00:18:49.230 --> 00:18:52.570
<i>So if I call him loudly enough, 
in the end, he'll definitely...</i>

00:18:56.160 --> 00:18:57.320
<i>That's right.</i>

00:18:58.030 --> 00:19:00.410
<i>If my voice isn't enough to be a guide now,</i>

00:19:00.960 --> 00:19:02.850
<i>it just has to become 
one good enough to do so!</i>

00:19:03.580 --> 00:19:06.580
<i>I just have to make him look my way again.</i>

00:19:06.970 --> 00:19:08.770
<i>You'd better prepare yourself, Momo.</i>

00:19:08.770 --> 00:19:10.600
<i>On May 29th,</i>

00:19:10.600 --> 00:19:14.300
<i>I'll call you with my loudest 
voice yet in these six years!</i>

00:19:19.970 --> 00:19:23.720
Yuzu

00:19:19.970 --> 00:19:23.720
Tomorrow at 6:00 PM, I want you to come to the 
N Building in West Shinjuku. I have something to say.

00:19:29.500 --> 00:19:31.090
This is Yuzu's.

00:19:31.090 --> 00:19:33.080
I'd better give it back when I see him.

00:19:34.360 --> 00:19:36.310
<i>I want to listen to that song again.</i>

00:19:37.220 --> 00:19:38.740
<i>I'm going to borrow it real quick!</i>

00:19:39.040 --> 00:19:42.610
<i>All right, we're going to start 
the "High School" demo.</i>

00:19:48.990 --> 00:19:52.090
<i>It's In NO Hurry's "High School."</i>

00:19:52.090 --> 00:19:54.630
<i>Huh? It's different from the CD.</i>

00:19:55.530 --> 00:19:56.600
<i>What is this?</i>

00:20:01.170 --> 00:20:02.130
<i>A studio?</i>

00:20:03.290 --> 00:20:06.090
<i>What does he want to talk to me about here?</i>

00:20:08.460 --> 00:20:09.520
<i>In NO Hurry.</i>

00:20:10.350 --> 00:20:12.110
<i>The vocalist, Alice.</i>

00:20:13.240 --> 00:20:14.280
<i>Could this be...</i>

00:20:19.750 --> 00:20:20.780
<i>It's that song!</i>

00:20:23.820 --> 00:20:25.260
Alice, listen.

00:20:25.260 --> 00:20:27.910
I made this song just because 
I wanted you to sing it.

00:20:28.540 --> 00:20:30.130
<i>Yuzu's in here.</i>

00:20:44.960 --> 00:20:46.030
<i>In NO Hurry!</i>

00:20:57.220 --> 00:20:58.350
Is this real?

00:21:04.450 --> 00:21:07.240
You're twenty minutes late, Alice.

00:21:07.500 --> 00:21:08.300
Yuzu.

00:21:08.910 --> 00:21:12.250
If the voice you have now 
isn't enough to reach Momo,

00:21:12.890 --> 00:21:14.530
then just use In NO Hurry.

00:21:14.860 --> 00:21:17.410
If you want your voice to reach 
Momo, who's already a pro,

00:21:17.410 --> 00:21:21.370
then I think In NO Hurry is the 
best place for you to be.

00:21:23.030 --> 00:21:26.530
Alice, I want you to become 
the vocalist of In NO Hurry.

00:21:27.640 --> 00:21:31.400
Up until now, I was lip syncing 
to Miou's singing.

00:21:31.840 --> 00:21:33.270
But Miou left.

00:21:33.820 --> 00:21:35.160
So Alice,

00:21:35.160 --> 00:21:39.270
become an Alice who really 
sings for In NO Hurry.

00:21:39.770 --> 00:21:44.280
On May 29th, I want you to perform with 
us on the live <i>Music King</i> broadcast.

00:21:45.370 --> 00:21:47.090
But Yuzu, that day...

00:21:47.090 --> 00:21:49.010
I'm going to the audition.

00:21:47.090 --> 00:21:49.010
You can do it after the audition.

00:21:54.290 --> 00:21:57.310
Jeez, I thought I'd be the 
one to tell you that first.

00:21:57.310 --> 00:21:59.640
That's my line.

00:21:59.640 --> 00:22:01.750
I'll sing with all my might.

00:22:02.810 --> 00:22:08.220
Even if I know I'll fail, it seems 
I'm just no good at giving up, Yuzu.

00:22:08.580 --> 00:22:10.530
Same here, Alice.

00:22:11.250 --> 00:22:15.570
<i>That day, we who were 
hiding how we truly felt</i>

00:22:15.570 --> 00:22:16.980
<i>joined hands.</i>

00:23:47.090 --> 00:23:52.280
♭05 I Wouldn't Have Had to 
See You Smile Like That
